<hr data-start="1389" data-end="1392">
<h2 data-section-id="1c2n1rd" data-start="1394" data-end="1414">🧠 Why this works</h2>
<ul data-start="1416" data-end="1562">
<li data-section-id="1uu9luq" data-start="1416" data-end="1457">
<p data-start="1418" data-end="1457"><code data-start="1418" data-end="1432">multi_cell()</code> resets X automatically</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="xctrk7" data-start="1458" data-end="1507">
<p data-start="1460" data-end="1507">BUT <code data-start="1464" data-end="1472">cell()</code> does NOT always reset X properly</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1ye4hdd" data-start="1508" data-end="1562">
<p data-start="1510" data-end="1562">So mixing them without <code data-start="1533" data-end="1542">set_x()</code> causes layout drift</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1564" data-end="1567">
